MEMORANDUM
TO:

Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:

TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:

October 2, 2023
SUBJECT:
Consideration of Bid #E-4-24 for furnishing Sixteen (16) New 4 Door 2023/2024
Model Utility Police Interceptors (SUV) for the Cheyenne Police Department
 ______________________________________________
Bid #E-4-24 was solicited for furnishing Sixteen (16) New 4 Door 2023/2024 Model Utility Police
Interceptors (SUV).

Three (3) bidders responded to this bid, and the bid tabulation is attached.  The Bids were received
from:
1. Dana Safety Supply

2. Ken Garff Cheyenne

3. Young Ford Ogden

The bids were reviewed by Joel Hickerson (CPD) and Bryan Bell (Fleet Maintenance) and their
recommendation is to accept the lowest responsive bid from Ken Garff Cheyenne.

Although Ken Garff Cheyenne is not the outright lowest bid submitted, Ken Garff Cheyenne was
the only Certified Resident Contractor.  As such, after application of the 5% Residency Preference,
Ken Garff is lowest responsive bidder.

The Bidding Documents contain a Surcharge and Escalator – Special Provision, for an amount
not-to-exceed Fifteen Percent (15%), of the total value of  requested items on the Bid.
The total Bid Award amount is $1,273,931.00 + Potential Future Surcharge Contingency
$191,089.65, for a grand total of $1,465,020.65.

Funding:
GL Totals w/o Surcharge Contingency
210-21-2111-40-85465 (Insurance Proceeds)

$125,702.00

020-26-2613-41-43201 (1% Sales Tax 19-22 / Motor Vehicles)
$1,148,229.00

Grand Total
$1,273,931.00
```

